From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: winex11: windows have no background, so they do not flash black

David: "sometimes windows flash black on open". winex11 created every window
with a black background pixel, so the X server painted a window black the
moment it was shown and before Wine drew it. With no background (None) the
server leaves what is under the window until its first paint -- Windows never
shows a window it has not drawn.

Gate: make test-blackflash (Wine stopped, so only the X server draws: a window
shown again is not black; what a hidden one uncovers is not black).
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -476,13 +476,18 @@
     attr->bit_gravity       = NorthWestGravity;
     attr->backing_store     = NotUseful;
     attr->border_pixel      = 0;
-    attr->background_pixel  = 0;
+    /* Stained Glass OS: no background -- the X server filled every new or
+     * newly shown window black until Wine painted it, a black flash each time
+     * a window opened (David 2026-09-29). With None the server leaves what is
+     * under the window until its first paint, as Windows never shows a window
+     * it has not drawn. */
+    attr->background_pixmap = None;
     attr->event_mask        = (ExposureMask | PointerMotionMask |
                                ButtonPressMask | ButtonReleaseMask | EnterWindowMask |
                                KeyPressMask | KeyReleaseMask | FocusChangeMask |
                                KeymapStateMask | StructureNotifyMask | PropertyChangeMask);
 
-    return (CWOverrideRedirect | CWSaveUnder | CWColormap | CWBorderPixel | CWBackPixel |
+    return (CWOverrideRedirect | CWSaveUnder | CWColormap | CWBorderPixel | CWBackPixmap |
             CWEventMask | CWBitGravity | CWBackingStore);
 }
 
